  "term": "LAMP",
  "definition": "LAMP refers to loop-mediated isothermal amplification, a rapid, low-resource method for amplifying DNA. In this source, it is discussed in a machine-learning context where digital images of LAMP test tubes are automatically classified as positive or negative to reduce errors from subjective visual reading.",
